[105.291, "o", "\u001b[0;36m\u001b[1mFounder:\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1;37m\u001b[1mZachary Winn\u001b[0m - Solo Founder\r\n  • Infrastructure & Security Engineer\r\n  • AWS & Cloudflare infrastructure experience\r\n  • Rust systems programming\r\n  • ARM64 security focus\r\n  • Learning binary exploitation & reverse engineering\r\n  \u001b[2mBased in Austin, TX\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[106.295333, "o", "\u001b[0;36m\u001b[1mWhat I'm Looking For:\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1;33m\u001b[1mOption 1: Technical Co-Founder\u001b[0m\r\n  • Security researcher with malware analysis experience\r\n  • Or experienced systems/infra engineer\r\n  • Equity split negotiable based on contribution\r\n  • Remote-friendly, prefer Austin area\r\n\r\n\u001b[1;33m\u001b[1mOption 2: Seed Funding ($500K-2M)\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[1;33mUse of Funds:\u001b[0m\r\n    • $400K-800K - Engineering team (2-3 engineers)\r\n    • $200K-400K - Security lab & testing infrastructure\r\n    • $100K-300K - Sales & marketing (first enterprise customers)\r\n    • $100K-200K - Certifications (SOC 2, penetration testing)\r\n    • $100K-300K - Operations & runway\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1;33mRealistic 18-Month Goals:\u001b[0m\r\n    • Build functional enterprise product\r\n    • 10-25 paying customers\r\n    • 1,000-3,000 managed endpoints\r\n    • $500K-1.5M ARR\r\n    • SOC 2 Type I in progress\r\n    • Validated detection on real malware\r\n\r\n\u001b[1;33m\u001b[1mOption 3: Strategic Partnership\u001b[0m\r\n  • Security firm with malware analysis capability\r\n  • Cloud provider interested in ARM64 security\r\n  • Existing EDR vendor looking for ARM64 solution\r\n\r\n"]
[108.29978, "o", "\u001b[0;35m\u001b[1m═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[0;36m\u001b[1mWhy ARM64 Security Matters:\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[0;32m1.\u001b[0m \u001b[1;37mARM64 is growing fast in enterprise\u001b[0m\r\n   • AWS Graviton instances are cheaper + more efficient\r\n   • Apple Silicon corporate adoption increasing\r\n   • Edge computing predominantly ARM64\r\n\r\n\u001b[0;32m2.\u001b[0m \u001b[1;37mCurrent solutions are inadequate\u001b[0m\r\n   • Most AV vendors just ported x86 code\r\n   • Memory vulnerabilities still plague the industry\r\n   • ARM64-specific threats are under-addressed\r\n\r\n\u001b[0;32m3.\u001b[0m \u001b[1;37mWindow of opportunity exists\u001b[0m\r\n   • No dominant ARM64-native security player yet\r\n   • Open-source builds credibility\r\n   • First-mover advantage still available\r\n\r\n"]
